   :approximate-date -2250 ;
   :material-note "Wood" ;
   :note "From Wikipedia: “The Dagenham idol is a wooden statue of a naked human figure, found in Dagenham, Essex, England in 1922. It it one of only a handful of prehistoric human-shaped wooden sculptures from the British Isles. The statue has been carbon dated to around 2250 BC, during the late Neolithic period or early Bronze Age, making it one of the oldest human representations found in England.”" ;
   :in-modern-country-note "England" ;
