   :material-note "Ceramic" ;
   :height 0.34 ;
   :apparent-gender :female ;
   :note "From Wikipedia: “The Masked Goddess (仮面の女神, Kamen no Megami) is a relatively large Japanese dogū or clay figurine of the late Jōmon period (c. 2000–1000 BC). Excavated from the Nakappara Site in Chino, Nagano Prefecture, it is exhibited at the nearby Togariishi Museum of Jōmon Archaeology. ... it is one of five dogū that have been designated National Treasures. ... The hollow figurine takes its name from the tilted, triangular mask that covers the face, with lines on top resembling the string with which such a mask might be tied on—or her eyebrows.”" ;
