   rdfs:label "San Lorenzo Colossal Head 5" ;
   :described-by <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olmec_colossal_heads> ;
   :earliest-date -1200 ;
   :latest-date -900 ;
   :in-modern-country-note "Mexico" ;
   :material-note "Basalt" ;
   :note "From Wikipedia: “The monument stands 1.86 metres (6.1 ft) high and measures 1.47 metres (4.8 ft) wide by 1.15 metres (3.8 ft) deep. It weighs 11.6 tons. The head was discovered by Matthew Stirling in 1946, face down in a gully to the south of the principal mound. The head is particularly well executed and is likely to have been found close to its original location. … The headdress is decorated with jaguar paws … At the back of the head, ten interlaced strips form a net decorated with disc motifs.”" ;
   :representative-latlong-point (17.7544 -94.7331) ; # San Lorenzo Tenochtitlán, Veracruz
   :wikimedia-commons-image-page <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cabeza_Colosal_5.jpg> .

