      <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Venta> ;
   :earliest-date -1000 ;
   :latest-date -600 ;
   :in-modern-country-note "Mexico" ;
   :material-note "Basalt" ;
   :note "From Wikipedia: “La Venta Monument 1 is speculated to have been the portrait of La Venta's final ruler. Monument 1 measures 2.41 metres (7.9 ft) high by 2.08 metres (6.8 ft) wide by 1.95 metres (6.4 ft) deep; it weighs 24 tons. … Monument 1 is the best preserved head at La Venta. … The head was first described by Franz Blom and Oliver La Farge who investigated the La Venta remains on behalf of Tulane University in 1925. … Matthew Stirling fully excavated the monument in 1940. … The head was found in its original context; associated finds have been radiocarbon dated to between 1000 and 600 BC.”" ;
   :representative-latlong-point (18.1031 -94.0392) ; # La Venta archaeological site, Tabasco
   :wikimedia-commons-image-page <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Olmeca_head_in_Villahermosa.jpg> .

