:nikandre-kore a :human-figure ;
   rdfs:label "Nikandre Kore" ;
   :described-by <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dedication_of_Nikandre> ;
   :approximate-date -650 ;
   :in-modern-country-note "Greece" ;
   :material-note "Naxian marble" ;
   :height 1.80 ;
   :apparent-gender :female ;
   :note "From Wikipedia: “The Dedication of Nikandre is a Greek marble sculpture, made approximately around 650 BCE, held in the National Archaeological Museum, Athens, Greece (Inv. 1). Nikandre, a woman from the island of Naxos, dedicated the statue in the temple of Artemis at Delos, the birthplace of Apollo and Artemis. The statue, which was found during archaeological excavation in the 19th century, is one of the earliest surviving korai, or statues of women, and displays one of the oldest inscriptions of Ancient Greek in stone. ... On the left side of the statue is the dedicatory inscription, one of the earliest surviving inscriptions of Greek in stone.”" ;
   :representative-latlong-point (37.3993075 25.268868) ; # TO CONFIRM: source unknown (Wikipedia's Delos coord is 37.39333333 25.27111111)
   :wikimedia-commons-image-page <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statue_of_Nikandre.jpg> .

:macmillan-aryballos a :group-of-human-figures ;
