   :note "Summarized from Spanish Wikipedia: Aristocratic warrior in combat from the Cerrillo Blanco sculptural ensemble at Porcuna; the surviving fragment (105 × 17 × 32 cm) preserves head, torso, and parts of the left arm and right thigh, wearing two superimposed cuirasses and a helmet with crest in the form of a feline. The sword and circular shield (caetra) would have been held in the right and left hands. Now displayed at the Museo Íbero de Jaén." ;
   :in-modern-country-note "Spain" ;
   :representative-latlong-point (37.869881 -4.184657) ;
