:statue-of-bes-fordongianus a :human-figure ;
   rdfs:label "Statue of Bes from Fordongianus" ;
   :described-by <https://virtualarchaeology.sardegnacultura.it/index.php/en/archaeological-sites/eta-fenicio-punica/fordongianus/finds/41-statue-of-bes> ;
   :earliest-date -300 ;
   :latest-date 100 ;
   :material-note "Stone" ;
   :apparent-gender :male ;
   :in-modern-country-note "Italy" ;
   :note "From Sardegna Cultura Virtual Archaeology: “The statue (fig. 1) smaller than the real one and with its head missing, portrays Bes, a minor divinity passed from the Egyptian pantheon to the Punic and then the Roman one. The god is portrayed as an obese midget with large feet, and is a beneficial, healthy divinity, assimilated to the god Aesclapius. The only garment worn is a skirt falling to the ankles, held at the waist by a twisted, knotted belt, with a wide band going downwards.” From the Roman baths of Forum Traiani (Fordongianus)." ;
   :representative-latlong-point (39.997264 8.80816) ; # ll for Terme di Fordongianus (Forum Traiani), from it.wikipedia
   :thumbnail-image <https://virtualarchaeology.sardegnacultura.it/images/romano/fordongianus/gd/98_pic.jpg> .

