   :note "From Wikipedia: “The Usuki Stone Buddhas is a group of 61 religious statues in four groups carved in bas-relief into a tuff cliff in the city of Usuki, Ōita Prefecture on the island of Kyushu, Japan. ... There are no historical materials remaining that testify to the period or circumstances surrounding the construction of these statues. ... However, based on the style, it is estimated that most of the statues were made in the late Heian period, and some in the Kamakura period.”" ;
