:madonna-bordone a :group-of-human-figures ;
   rdfs:label "Madonna del Bordone" ;
   :described-by <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madonna_del_Bordone> ;
   :approximate-date 1261 ;
   :in-modern-country-note "Italy" ;
   :material-note "Tempera on panel" ;
   :height 2.25 ;
   :apparent-gender :female , :male ;
   :note "From Wikipedia: “The Madonna del Bordone (‘The Madonna of the pilgrim's staff’) is a panel painting by the Italian painter Coppo di Marcovaldo, in the church of Santa Maria dei Servi in Siena, Italy. Signed and dated 1261, the work is the only certain attribution to the Florentine painter. ... It portrays the Madonna enthroned with a halo and two small angels on her sides. She is enthroned, and supports the blessing Child, who is holding the Book of the Law in his left hand and has a halo surrounded by a jewelled cross.”" ;
   :representative-latlong-point (43.315327 11.338174) ; # Santa Maria dei Servi, Siena, from Wikipedia
   :wikimedia-commons-image-page <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coppo_di_marcovaldo,_madonna_del_bordone,_siena,_chiesa_dei_servi,_1261_tavola,.jpg> .

:coronation-virgin-santa-maria-maggiore a :group-of-human-figures ;
   rdfs:label "Coronation of the Virgin, Apse Mosaic, Santa Maria Maggiore" ;
   :described-by <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santa_Maria_Maggiore> ,
      <https://www.visualmuseum.gallery/gallery/coronation-of-the-virgin-closeup/> ;
   :approximate-date 1295 ;
   :in-modern-country-note "Italy" ;
   :material-note "Mosaic" ;
   :apparent-gender :female , :male ;
   :note "From Wikipedia: “The apse mosaic, the Coronation of the Virgin, is from 1295, signed by the Franciscan friar, Jacopo Torriti.” ... From Visual Museum website: “The pair are dressed in gold, sitting upon a throne in the heavenlies (stars, sun, and moon against dark blue background). Jesus places crown upon Mary; in his left hand a book. Mary's hands are raised in prayer. Throngs of angels on either side with Peter, Paul, and Francis on the left, John the Baptist, John the Evangelist, and Anthony on the right.”" ;
   :representative-latlong-point (41.8975 12.49861111) ; # Santa Maria Maggiore, Rome, from Wikipedia
   :wikimedia-commons-image-page <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jacopo_torriti,_coronation_of_the_virgin,_santa_maria_maggiore,_rome.jpg> .

